# mem_block_dies.tkr — the C-route regressor of `if`-ARM block-local str residence (0.3.1
# modelo-de-memoria-por-escopo §4/§9, crumb C3).
#
# WHAT IT PINS. The five lexical scopes (bare block / loop / if-arm / when-arm / fn) are treated
# identically by the model: a local proven block-local dies at its scope's exit edge. Here a `str`
# built inside an `if` arm and consumed with a non-tail, non-assign-RHS use is proven block-local by
# the residence oracle and routed through `tk_str_concat_r(<arm region>, …)` (codegen crumb C3), so
# its buffer dies when the arm closes.
#
# WHAT IT PROVES. `tag_in_arm` emits its arm-scoped `arm-value` token, then `churn` opens and closes
# eight further allocating scopes that recycle the arm's freed region memory. The `arm-value` token
# must still read back exactly — a use-after-drop of the arm-scoped buffer would corrupt it, not
# merely leak it. The contiguous line is the witness.
#
# C ROUTE by construction: `Given env = ["TEKO_BACKEND=c"]` pins the shared build to the C backend,
# the route crumb C3 activates the scope routing on. The native route inherits the same lifecycle
# once crumb C4 lands and unlocks the native gate.

Feature: mem_block_dies — an if-arm block-local str dies at the arm exit yet reads back exactly

  Scenario: an arm-scoped str reads back its exact value across the post-arm scope churn
    Given env = ["TEKO_BACKEND=c"]
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "arm-value[|]ok"
